      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Club return",
          "heading": "Jack Singleton scores on Glasgow debut after cardiac event; Warriors beat Lions",
          "body": "Jack Singleton marked his Glasgow debut with a try in the 35th minute as the Warriors beat the Lions 28-20 at Scotstoun, keeping their unbeaten run alive. The 30-year-old, a former England hooker, had a cardiac event during training at Gloucester last year and had stents and balloons fitted, and this was his first appearance in 13 months. Fergus Watson opened the scoring as the Warriors led 19-3 at half-time, before the Lions fought back in the second half."
        },
