      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Contract news",
          "heading": "Wales wing Ellis Mee signs new Scarlets contract, length undisclosed",
          "body": "Ellis Mee has committed his future to Scarlets with a new contract, though the length of the deal has not been disclosed. The 23-year-old has made 43 appearances for the region since arriving from Nottingham in 2024, scoring 11 tries, and has 11 Test caps for Wales since his debut against Ireland in the 2025 Six Nations. Scarlets director of rugby Nigel Davies called him an exciting player and a great character within the group. Mee is in Steve Tandy's squad for the Nations Championship games."
        },
