        {
          "kicker": "Selection call",
          "heading": "Sir John Kirwan urges Rennie to use Ma'u and Tosi's size",
          "body": "Sir John Kirwan, speaking on the Rivals podcast, wants the All Blacks to play more size up front, especially against South Africa. Saula Ma'u and Pasilio Tosi are both around 22st, and Ma'u came into the 36-man squad after Tyrel Lomax was ruled out with a neck issue. Kirwan conceded they may not yet be the best in their position, but said: \"I do think we need their size.\" Ma'u, who has yet to earn a cap, impressed in the tour game against the Lions."
        },
